-- =========================
--  Starts automatically on load. Home toggles it on/off.
--
--  Flow:
--    1. Wait for RoundStart (or detect the round already in progress).
--    2. Hide under the map while idle (no candy / waiting for role).
--    3. As soon as candy exists, walk to the nearest safe candy. Exact-distance
--       ties use a stable per-object key so the picker cannot flip back and
--       forth. Movement uses Roblox's TweenService at the configured speed.
--       Non-murderers ignore candy within 10 studs horizontally and 10 studs
--       above or below the murderer.
--    4. The candy bag GUI counter is the authority: combat starts only when
--       the visible "Coins" counter under ...CoinBags.Container.Candy says 50.
--         Innocent -> fling sheriff -> grab dropped gun -> sync-shoot murderer
--         Sheriff  -> sync 3 studs behind murderer, hold for 1s, fire at 0.5s
--         Murderer -> set everyone's hitbox to 500 -> equip knife -> use knife's
--                     HandleTouched remote on everyone
--
--  Movement anchors the root only for the first 80% of each TweenService leg
--  (this locks the vertical axis and prevents jitter), then unanchors so touch
--  pickups can register during the final approach. A missed gun volley hides
--  under the map and idles for 4 seconds before the next attempt.
--
--  If you get kicked, the script rejoins the same server, queues the loader
--  URL, and re-executes on the new server. If that same round is still live
--  and the murderer is alive, it flings him after rejoining. If no round
--  starts for 90 seconds, it hops to a half-full server with the lowest ping.
--  If you die while farming with an unfinished bag, it flings the murderer
--  after you respawn so the round ends.
-- =========================

